<article class="env-lemma" id="04MV">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04MV">Lemma <span data-tag="04MV">40.9.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $(U, R, s, t, c)$ be a groupoid scheme over $S$. Let $g : U' \to U$ be a morphism of schemes. Let $(U', R', s', t', c')$ be the restriction of $(U, R, s, t, c)$ via $g$, and let $h = s \circ \text{pr}_1 : U' \times _{g, U, t} R \to U$. If $\mathcal{P}$ is a property of morphisms of schemes such that </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$h$ has property $\mathcal{P}$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\mathcal{P}$ is preserved under base change, 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> then $s', t'$ have property $\mathcal{P}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is clear as $s'$ is the base change of $h$ by Diagram (<a href="/tag/04MN" data-tag="04MN">40.9.0.1</a>) and $t'$ is isomorphic to $s'$ as a morphism of schemes. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>